Today is Sunday.
It is a calm morning here in Kochi.
There is a small bakery near my flat.
I walk there.
The bakery is very busy.
The shopkeeper is very busy.
I look into the glass display case.
There are a lot of sweets there.
"Who is next?" the shopkeeper asks.
"This is my turn," I say.
"What is your order?" he asks.
I point to the red halwa.
"I want a small box of halwa," I say.
He quickly takes a small box.
